// GEMV demo program: exactly 11 explicit WRSR instructions, one GEMV, HALT.
// The testbench reads this file at run time; no RTL rebuild is needed.
//
// Format: exactly two hex digits per byte token. Whitespace is ignored;
// // or # starts a comment through end-of-line. Bytes are packed
// little-endian into 32-bit PMEM words (byte 0 -> bits 7:0).
//
// PC  bytes       field
//  0  60 00 00    WRSR r0  activation_base = 0 (HFC source, chunk 0)
//  3  61 00 00    WRSR r1  weight_base[15:0] = 0
//  6  62 01 00    WRSR r2  tile_count = 1 (one 128-row output tile)
//  9  63 08 00    WRSR r3  chunks_per_tile = 8 (8 x 16 = 128 inputs)
// 12  64 08 00    WRSR r4  chunks_per_scale_group = 8 (one scale group)
// 15  65 00 00    WRSR r5  output_base = 0 (first destination tile)
// 18  66 00 00    WRSR r6  weight_base[16] = 0
// 21  67 00 00    WRSR r7  scale_base[15:0] = 0
// 24  68 00 00    WRSR r8  scale_base[16] = 0
// 27  69 AD 0C    WRSR r9  = 0x0CAD: src=1 (HFC), dest=9 (QKV), qzero_raw=1, frac=13
// 30  6A 00 00    WRSR r10 output_conversion = 0 (destination-fixed conversion)
// 33  80          GEMV: run the latched configuration
// 34  40          HALT: freeze the PC here
//
// Safe edit for the walkthrough: change r9's immediate to 0x082D
// (69 2D 08) to route to destination 0 (Q) instead of QKV composite.
// The first tile still lands in q_full_buf[0], so the observed values match.
60 00 00
61 00 00
62 01 00
63 08 00
64 08 00
65 00 00
66 00 00
67 00 00
68 00 00
69 AD 0C
6A 00 00
80
40
